$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,7-dichlorodibenzo[b, f][1,4]oxazepin-11(10H)-one (46) Following the
general procedure II,
5-chloro-N-(4-chloro-2-hydroxyphenyl)-2-fluorobenzamide (30.0 mg, 0.1
mmol), K2CO3 (27.6 mg, 0.2 mmol) and 1.5 ml DMF were used. The reaction
mixture was stirred at 100 °C for 3h. After completion of the reaction,
the residue was purified by silical gel column chromatography (petroleum
ether: ethyl acetate = 5:1). Finally, compound (46) was isolated. (26 mg,
white solid), 92% yield. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 10.75 (s, 1H),
7.72-7.68 (m, 2H), 7.52 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.42 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H),
7.29 (dd, J = 8.6 Hz, 2.3Hz, 1H), 7.17 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H); 13C-NMR (100
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 162.1, 161.5, 159.7, 159.6, 159.5, 151.4, 134.2,
134.1, 131.5, 130.0, 128.6, 126.3, 123.1, 121.5, 116.7, 116.6, 115.2,
115.1, 114.1, 113.9; LRMS (ESI) calcd for C13H8Cl2NO2 [M+H]+: 279.99
found 280.01
