$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.2. General procedure for the synthesis of
2-phenoxybenzaldehydes 7a-7h (GP2): phenol (2.2 mmol, 1.2 equiv) and
anhydrous K2CO3 (2.20 mmol, 304 mg, 1.2 equiv) were added to a solution
of 2-fluorobenzaldehyde (2.00 mmol, 212 μL, 1.0 equiv) in DMA (3 mL) and
the resulting reaction mixture was slowly heated to 170 °C. After
stirring at that temperature for 4 h and cooling to room temperature the
reaction mixture was poured into H2O (10 mL) and the aqueous layer was
extracted with DCM (3 x20 mL). After drying over MgSO4, filtration and
concentration in vacuo the residue was purified by FC (P/MTBE) to afford
the desired 2-phenoxybenzaldehyde. With phenol (207 mg, 2.20 mmol, 1.2
equiv). With 2-fluoro-4-methoxybenzaldehyde (308 mg, 2.00 mmol, 1.0
equiv) instead of 2-fluorobenzaldehyde and p-methoxyphenol (273 mg, 2.20
mmol, 1.2 equiv). 4-Methoxy-2-(4-methoxyphenoxy)benzaldehyde (7f) as a
pale pink solid, yield 1.84 mmol, 475 mg, 92%. MP: 161 °C. IR (neat):
2957br w, 2869br w, 2839br w, 1680m, 1667m, 1599s, 1576s, 1499s, 1462m,
1445m, 1427m, 1401w, 1392m, 1335m, 1291m, 1259s, 1242s, 1207s, 1165s,
1152s, 1107s, 1092s, 1028s, 966m, 835s, 803s, 762m, 638m, 580m. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3, 300 K) δ = 10.38 (s, 1 H, CHO), 7.86 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1
H, CHarom), 7.02 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 2 H, CHarom), 6.91 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 2 H,
CHarom), 6.65 - 6.60 (m, 1 H, CHarom), 6.22 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H, CHarom),
3.80 (s, 3 H, CH3), 3.73 (s, 3 H, CH3). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, 300 K) δ
= 188.0 (CHO), 165.8 (C), 162.9 (C), 156.6 (C), 148.7 (C), 130.2 (CH),
121.2 (2 x CH), 119.9 (C), 115.1 (2 x CH), 108.6 (CH), 102.0 (CH), 55.6
(CH3), 55.5 (CH3). HRMS (ESI) m/z = 279.0628 calcd. for C15H12O4Na
[M+Na]+, found: 279.0633.
