$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for
CuI/N,N-dimethylglycine-Catalyzed Coupling Reaction of Aryl Iodides and
Phenols. A Schlenk tube was charged with aryl iodide (0.5 mmol), phenol
(0.75 mmol), CuI (0.15 mmol), N,N-dimethylglycine hydrochloride salt (0.5
mmol), Cs2CO3 (1.5 mmol), and 2 mL of 1, 4-dioxane, evacuated, and
backfilled with argon. The reaction mixture was stirred at 90 °C until
the conversion was completed as detected by TLC. The suspension was
filtered and the filtrate was concentrated, followed by column
chromatography on silica gel (eluting with 1:100 to 1:5 ethyl
acetate/petroleum ether) to provide the desired product.
(S)-3-[4-(4-Acetylphenoxy)phenyl]-2-(tritylamino)propionic Acid Methyl
Ester 8c. [α]D 25 +57.7 (c 1.0, CHCl3); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.94
(d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.43 (m, 6H), 7.20 (m, 11H), 7.00 (m, 4H), 3.61 (m,
1H), 3.06 (s, 3H), 2.97 (m, 2H), 2.65 (d, J = 11.1 Hz, 1H), 2.57 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 196.8, 174.8, 162.2, 154.3, 145.9, 134.0,
131.9, 131.5, 130.7, 128.9, 128.2, 127.9, 126.7, 126.5, 120.1, 117.2,
71.1, 58.3, 51.4, 41.7, 26.5; IR (film) 3317, 3057, 3021, 1738, 1681,
1594 cm-1; ESI-MS m/z 578.3 (M + Na)+; HRMS calcd for C37H33NO4Na (M +
Na)+ 578.2302, found 578.2301.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Ullman-type coupling, ee >99% (no racemization)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mild and Nonracemizing Conditions for Ullmann-type Diaryl Ether Formation
between Aryl Iodides and Tyrosine Derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cai, Qian; He, Gang; Ma, Dawei
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(14), 5268-5273

