$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of the N-methoxyethyl piperidine 4-fluorosulfone 22v (6.0
g, 16.0 mmol) and powdered K2CO3 (4.44 g, 32 mmol) in DMF (30 mL) was
added 4-(trifluoromethoxy)phenol (5.72 g, 32 mmol), and the mixture was
then heated to 90 °C for 25 h. The solution was concentrated under high
vacuum, and the residue was dissolved in EtOAc. This organic phase was
washed with 1N aqueous NaOH, water, and brine and dried over MgSO4.
Chromatography on silica gel eluting with EtOAc/ hexane provided the
trifluoromethoxy phenoxyphenyl sulfone 20v as a light-yellow gel (7.81 g,
91.5%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Orally Active MMP-1 Sparing α-Tetrahydropyranyl and α-Piperidinyl Sulfone
