$DATUM Method B. 2 K2CO3 (5.7 g, 41 mmol) was added to a solution of
2-iodophenol (4.5 g, 21 mmol) and
2-bromo-1-fluoro-4-(trifluormethyl)benzene (5.0 g, 21 mmol, purchased
from TCI) in DMSO (65 mL) and the suspension was stirred at 95 °C for 48
h, and then the reaction mixture was poured into water (100 mL). After
the extraction with EtOAc (3×30 mL) and drying over MgSO4 the solvent was
removed in vacuo. The crude product was then purified by column
chromatography (Hexane/EtOAc). The desired product as a colorless oil
(8.3 g, 19 mmol, 91%).
