$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Coupling Reaction of Diphenyl Ether
(under Microwave Irradiation) for 10a, 10c, 11c, and 11d. A mixture of
4-substituted N1-(4-cyanophenyl)-5-chloro-2-nitroaniline (1 equiv, 7 or
9) and para-substituted 2,6-dimethylphenol (1.2 equiv) in DMF (3 mL) in
the presence of anhydrous potassium carbonate (2 equiv) was irradiated
under microwave conditions with stirring at 190 °C for 15 min. The
mixture was poured into ice-water, adjusted to neutral pH with aqueous
HCl (5%), and extracted with EtOAc three times. After removal of organic
solvent under reduced pressure, crude product was purified by PTLC or
flash column chromatography (gradual eluant, petroleum ether/CH2Cl2).
N1-(4'-Cyanophenyl)-5-(2",6"-dimethyl-4"-nitrophenoxy)-4-trifluoromethyl-2-nitroaniline
(11d). Starting with 171 mg (0.5 mmol) of 7 and 100 mg (0.6 mmol) of
2,6-dimethyl-p-nitrophenol to afford 215 mg of 11d, yield 91%, yellow
solid. mp 240-242 °C; 1H NMR δ ppm 2.24 (6H, s, 2 × CH3), 6.22 (1H, s,
ArH-6), 7.10 (2H, d, J= 8.8 Hz, ArH-2',6'), 7.55 (2H, d, J= 8.8 Hz,
ArH-3',5'), 8.02 (2H, s, ArH-3",5"), 8.69 (1H, s, ArH-3), 9.92 (1H, s,
NH); MS m/z (%) 473.3 (M + 1, 100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design, Synthesis, and Preclinical Evaluations of Novel 4-Substituted
1,5-Diarylanilines as Potent HIV-1 Non-Nucleoside Reverse Transcriptase
Inhibitor (NNRTI) Drug Candidates
