$DATUM 2.2.3 4,5-Bis(4-nitrophenoxy)-2-phenyloxazole 4 16.2 g of 3, 29.9 g of
cesium fluoride and 4-fluoronitrobenzene 15.7 mL (0.142 mol) in NMP 115
mL were stirred at room temperature for 30 minutes. The temperature was
raised to 160 °C and refluxed for 3 h. The mixture was poured into water
to precipitate. The product was washed with hot water until the solution
became neutral, filtered and dried under reduced pressure at 80 °C
overnight. The product was recrystallized from water and dried under
reduced pressure for 48 h to afford needles 24.4 g of shiny
yellowneedles, yield of 91%. m.p. of 258 °C(DTA) E.A. calculated for
C33H21N3O7 (327.38) (%); C, 69.35; H, 3.70; N, 7.35. Found; C, 68.56; H,
3.66; N, 7.26. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) 7.28-7.34 (m, 8H ArH), 7.62-7.65
(m, 3H, ArH), 7.62-7.87 (m, 4H, ArH), 8.15-8.20 (m, 2H, ArH), 8.28-8.33
(m, 4H, ArH). IR (KBr, cm-1) 1344, 1510 (-NO2).
