$DATUM Methyl 4-chloro-3-nitrobenzoate (2.16 g, 10 mmol, 1 eq.) was mixed with
thymol (1.50 g, 10 mmol, 1 eq.) and K2CO3 (2.76 g, 20 mmol, 2 eq.) in DMF
(2 mL). The reaction was heated at 110°C for 2 h and then cooled down to
rt. After neutralization with 1 N HCl(aq), the reaction mixture was
extracted with CH2Cl2 (20 mL×3), dried over MgSO4, and purified by flash
column chromatography on silica, eluted with 30% ethyl acetate in
hexanes. SA-T-1 (3.01g, 91 %). 1H NMR (600 MHz,CDCl3) δ 1.16 (d, 6H, J =
7.2 Hz), 2.29 (s, 3H), 3.05 (m, 1H), 3.92 (s, 3H), 6.77 (s, 1H), 6.82 (d,
1H, J = 9.0 Hz), 7.06 (d, 1H, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.26 (d, 1H, J = 7.8 Hz), 8.05
(dd, 1H, J = 9.0, 1.8 Hz), 8.58 (d, 1H, J = 1.8 Hz).13C NMR (150 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 165.0, 155.5, 150.9, 139.8, 137.8, 137.7, 135.1, 127.7, 127.6,
127.5, 124.0, 121.4, 117.4, 52.7, 27.2, 23.2(×2), 21.0.
