$DATUM Synthesis of IV: Commercially available 2-fluoro-6-methoxybenzaldehyde
III (20.0 g, 130 mmol) and bis-phenol (16.8 g, 59.0 mmol) were dissolved
in DMF (59 mL). To the resulting solution was added K2CO3 (17.9 g, 130
mmol) and the mixture was stirred under reflux for 3 d. The reaction
mixture was quenched by the addition of H2O and the products were
extracted with CHCl3. The combined organic layer was washed with H2O,
brine and dried over MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
crude product was purified by the column chromatography (SiO2,
hexane/ethyl acetate =1/1) and concentrated in vacuo to give IV as white
powders (29.7 g, 91%). Mp: 101.6-103.0 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, 298 K, CDCl3)
δ 10.70 (s, CHO, 2H), 7.28 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 6.95 (s, 4H), 6.59 (d, J
= 8.4 Hz, 2H), 6.08 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 3.93 (m, 6H), 2.10 (s, 12H),
1.67 (s, 6H) ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, 298K, CDCl3) δ 189.0, 162.1, 160.9,
148.6, 147.9, 135.7, 130.4, 127.6, 114.1, 105.9, 104.5, 56.3, 42.2, 31.1,
16.2 ppm. IR (KBr): 2967, 2868, 1692, 1244, 1173 cm-1 FAB-HRMS, m/z
Calcd. for C35H37O6 [M+H]+ 553.2590; found 553.2585.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Main-Chain-Type Polyrotaxanes by New Click Polymerization
Using Homoditopic Nitrile N-Oxides via Rotaxanation-Polymerization
Protocol
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lee, Young-Gi; Koyama, Yasuhito; Yonekawa, Morio; Takata, Toshikazu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
