$DATUM 4-(2-Methoxycarbonyl-phenoxy)-3-nitro-benzoic acid ethyl ester. To a
stirred solution of ethyl 4-fluoro-3-nitrobenzoate (2.53 g, 11.87 mmol)
in DMF (40 mL) containing Cs2CO3 (4.26 g, 13.06 mmol) at 100°C was added
drop wise methyl salicylate (1.69 mL, 13.06 mol) dissolved in DMF (40 mL)
over 2h. After 15 min the reaction mixture was allowed to reach rt and
then diluted with ethyl acetate (100 mL) and washed with water (2 x 100
mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with dichloromethane (100 mL).
Drying (MgSO4) of the combined organic layers followed by filtration,
concentration in vacuo and purification by silica gel column
chromatography using ethyl acetate (0-40%) in heptane provided the title
compound (3.75 g, 91%) as a yellow solid
4-(2-Methoxycarbonyl-phenoxy)-3-nitro-benzoic acid ethyl ester, (3.75 g,
91%) yield 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.60 (m, 1H), 8.07 - 8.02 (m, 2H),
7.62 (ddd, 1H, J = 2.0, 7.6, 8.2), 7.38 (ddd, 1H, J = 1.2, 7.6, 7.8),
7.21 (dd, 1H, J = 1.0, 8.2), 6.73 (d, 1H, J = 8.2), 4.37 (q, 2H, J =
7.1), 3.71 (s, 3H), 1.38 (t, 3H, J = 7.1); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
164.9, 164.4, 155.3, 153.2, 139.8, 135.1, 134.6, 133.0, 127.5, 126.5,
124.8, 124.0, 123.4, 117.1, 61.8, 52.5, 14.5
