$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2 Synthesis of intermediates 1a-1h 0.11 mol
substituted phenol was added into a 250 mL three-neck flask equipped with
a thermometer and a reflux condenser tube and melted by heating. 0.10 mol
KOH was added. The mixture was stirred until the formed water was
completely evaporated. 0.09 mol p-chloronitrobenzene was then added. The
reaction was heated to 150 °C and conducted for 1-4 h. The reaction
endpoint was detected by TLC. Upon completion, the reaction system was
washed three times by adding 5 % NaOH solution at 100 °C then water at
the same temperature until pH value reached neutrality. The resulting
solution was poured into cold water to cool, filtered and dried to give
yellow intermediate 1a-1h[14, 15] (yield 75 %-90 %). 1f, 90 %, yellow
product
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
