$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-chloro-1-fluorodibenzo[b, f][1,4]oxazepin-11(10H)-one (39) Following
the general procedure II,
N-(4-chloro-2-hydroxyphenyl)-2,6-difluorobenzamide (28.3 mg, 0.1 mmol),
K2CO3 (27.6 mg, 0.2 mmol) and 1.5 ml DMF were used. The reaction mixture
was stirred at 100 °C for 3h. After completion of the reaction, the
residue was purified by silical gel column chromatography (petroleum
ether: ethyl acetate = 5:1). Finally, compound (39) was isolated. (23 mg,
white solid), 90% yield. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 11.08 (s, 1H),
7.72-7.68 (m, 2H), 7.52 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.42 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H),
7.29 (dd, J = 8.6 Hz, 2.3Hz, 1H), 7.17 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H); 13C-NMR (100
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ (ppm) 164.1, 157.0, 150.34, 134.17, 130.6, 130.0, 129.8,
127.1, 126.2, 122.88, 122.87, 121.5; LRMS (ESI) calcd for C13H8ClFNO2
[M+H]+: 264.01 found 264.05
