$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 4-(9-anthryl)-2,6-bis[4-(4'-nitrophenoxy)phenyl]pyridine
(ABNPP) To a 250 ml three-necked round bottomed flask equipped with a
nitrogen inlet, Dean-Stark trap and a condenser, were added 6.58 g (0.015
mol) of 4-anthryl-2,6-bis(4- hydroxyphenyl)pyridine, p-chloronitrobenzene
(5.024 g, 0.032 mol), anhydrous potassium carbonate (4.416 g, 0.032 mol),
and DMAc (20 ml). After the mixture was stirred for 1 h, 35 ml of dry
toluene was added, the reaction temperature was raised slowly and the
generated water was removed from the reaction mixture by azeotropic
distillation. The reaction temperature was raised to 155 °C and kept at
the temperature for 20 h. The resultant reaction mixture was cooled and
poured into ice-cold water. The precipitate was filtered and dried in
vacuum oven at 60 °C. The crude product was purified by recrystallisation
from 2-methoxy ethanol. Pale yellow crystals. Yield: 90%. FT-IR (KBr,
cm-1 ); 1,531 and 1,343 cm-1 (asymmetric and symmetric stretching
vibration of -NO2 group), 1,245 cm-1 (C-O-C stretching vibration). 1H-NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, ppm); δ -8.19 (s, 1H, 1), 7.71 (d, 4H, 2), 7.52 (t, 4H,
3), 8.01 (s, 2H, 4), 8.10 (d, 4H, 5), 6.89 (d, 4H, 6), 7.11 (d, 4H, 7),
8.24 (d, 4H, 8). 13C-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, ppm); δ -C1 -125.9, C2 -131.6,
C3 -129.7, C4 -125.8, C5 - 130.2, C6 -135.7, C7 -151.2, C8 -118.5, C9
-159.2, C10 -132.4, C11 -127.2, C12 -118.1, C13 -155.1, C14 - 162.2, C15
-119.7, C16 -124.3, C17 -142.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and characterization of pyridine and anthracene containing
bismaleimides, bisnadimides and polyaspartimides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Amutha, N.; Sarojadevi, M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Polymer Research (2008), 15(6), 487-499

