$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2,3,5,6-Tetrafluoro-4-(4-formyl-2-methoxyphenoxy)benzaldehyde (18).
4-Hydroxy-3-methoxybenzaldehyde (7; 761 mg, 5 mmol) and
pentafluorobenzaldehyde (1; 0.615 mL, 5 mmol) were dissolved in DMF (5
mL) and KF (0.581 g, 10 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was stirred
at r.t. for 3 h. The mixture was poured into H2O (30 mL) and extracted
with EtOAc (2 × 30 mL). The organic layer was washed with H2O (2 × 50
mL), dried (Na2SO4) and filtered, then concentrated to dryness and
chromatographed (EtOAc-hexanes, 1:9 to 2.5:7.5) to give pure product,
that was crystallized (EtOAc-hexanes). Oil, yield 1.47 g, 90%. Mp
96.2-96.9 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 3.93 (s, 3 H), 7.16 (d, J =
8.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.48 (dd, J = 1.8, 1.9 Hz, 1 H), 7.54 (d, J = 1.8 Hz, 1 H),
9.95 (s, 1 H), 10.29 (t, J = 0.1 Hz, 1 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
56.3, 110.7, 111.2, 117.9, 125.1, 134.1, 139.6, 140.7, 147.3, 149.6,
150.3, 181.9, 190.5. HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for C15H8F4O4: 328.03587;
found: 328.03505. Anal. Calcd for C15H8F4O4: C, 54.89; H, 2.46; F, 23.15.
Found: C, 54.85; H, 2.59; F, 23.17.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Straightforward transformation of pentafluorobenzaldehyde into
4-aryloxy-2,3,5,6-tetrafluorobenzaldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gryko, Daniel T.; Wyrostek, Dagmara; Nowak-Krol, Agnieszka; Abramczyk,
Katarzyna; Rogacki, Maciej K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2008), (24), 4028-4032

