$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Microwave Synthesis of
2-Hydroxy Diaryl Ethers (1-6) Cesium carbonate (1.5 mM) and appropriate
phenol (1.5 mM) were taken in 5 ml of NMP. The slurry was stirred at room
temp for 45 minutes. To this reaction mixture 2-bromo-4-chlorophenol (1
mM) and Cu(I) chloride (0.25 mM) was added. This reaction mixture was
irradiated under microwave for 5 minutes (2 min, 2 min and 1 min) at
power of 500W (WB 23SG1) to get desired compounds (1-6). After cooling
the reaction mixture it was 10 times diluted with ethyl acetate washed
with water and brine and organic layer was dried over sodium sulphate.
The product was purified by 100-200 mesh silica gel column chromatography
(5-50% ethyl acetate in petroleum ether). The products were characterized
by 1H NMR, 13C NMR (JEOL 300 MHz spectrometer), mass spectra and CHN
analysis, which were found in full agreement with microwave as well as
conventional method. Preparation of
4-Chloro-2-(5-chloroquinolin-8-yl)oxy]phenol (4). It was prepared from
2-bromo-4-chlorophenol and 5-chloro-8-hydroxyquinoline in 90% isolated
yield (off white powder) after purification from silica gel column
chromatography using 12% ethyl acetate in petroleum ether. 1H NMR (CDCl3)
δ 8.9 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H); 8.63 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H); 7.64-7.56 (m, 3H);
7.23 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H); 7.01 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H); 6.80 (d, J = 8.4 Hz,
1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 153.09, 150.68, 149.66, 144.72, 141.17, 134.70,
132.32, 131.20, 127.28, 122.83, 122.50, 120.02, 119.91, 118.81, 115.93.
MS m/z found 306.1, Calculated for C15H9O2NCl2 306.15. CHN analysis found
C, 58.38; H, 3.07; N, 4.56; for C15H9O2NCl2 calculated C, 58.85; H, 2.96;
N, 4.58. M.P. (uncorrected) 126-128°C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation ((2nd stage)), alternative reaction conditions gave
lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-step synthesis of novel antimicrobial 2-hydroxy diaryl ethers through
domestic microwave heating
