$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of bromobenzene (0.07 mL, 0.4 mmol),
potassium phenoxide (125 mg, 1.0 mmol), CuCl (40 mg, 0.4 mmol) in
[bmim][BF4] (2.0 mL) was heated at 100°C with stirring for 10 h under
nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction was monitored by GC and TLC and the
product was extracted with ethyl acetate:hexane. (3 x 10 mL, 1:1 v/v).
The product was purified by column chromatography to give diphenyl ether
in 72% yield and was characterized by comparison, with authentic sample
(b.p., GC) and other spectroscopic data such as 1H NMR, IR, and EI-MS.
Similarly, other diaryl ethers were prepared by the reaction.
p-methoxyphenyl p-nitrophenylether, yield 90%. M.p./b.p.(°C)
(Lit.m.p./b.p.)ref: 110-113g (110-111)[29].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM ionic liq., [bmim][PF6] alternately used as solvent with same yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper(I) chloride catalyzed synthesis of diaryl ethers in ionic liquids
under mild conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
